import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableRotation
import AxQM.Core.QtowerSingleWireGate

/-!
# The reachable rotation tower gates, over the named gates `H, S`
(N&C Exercise 4.43, named-gate re-expression of the rotation family)

The universality argument of Exercise 4.43 shows the **operator density on the
control tower**:
`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableTowerDensity.lean`) shows that, up to a global phase, every
tower evolution is a limit of the operators of the tower circuit submonoid
`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ`. That submonoid has two generating families
(`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableCircuitTower.lean`):

* the single-tower-wire reachable single-qubit rotations `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E`
  (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`), and
* the `≤ 2`-control reversible tower gates `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht`.

For the *named* four-gate universality conclusion, these generating gates must be re-expressed
over the four **named** gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` (with the
measurement-realised `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` for the irrational `R_z(θ)`). **This file does it for
the rotation family**: it shows every reachable single-qubit rotation gate — and its placement on a
tower wire — is generated by the two named gates `hadamardGate`, `sGate` together with the single
non-Clifford base rotation `rotZGate θ` (the gate the Exercise 4.41 measurement circuit
`rzThreeFifthsCircuit` realises, on its success branch, `rzThreeFifthsCircuit_success_eq_rotZ`).

## What is formalised

* `reachableRotationGates_le_closure_named` — **the single-qubit re-expression.** The reachable
  single-qubit rotation submonoid is contained in the submonoid generated by
  `{hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`:

    `reachableRotationGates θ ≤ Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`.

  Each of the four generators `R_z(±θ), R_x(±θ)` is a finite composition of `H`, `S`, and the base
  rotation `R_z(θ)`: `R_z(θ)` is a generator; `R_z(-θ) = (H·S²·H)·R_z(θ)·(H·S²·H)`
  (`rotZGate_neg_eq_hadamardGate_sGate_conj`, using the `{H, S}` circuit `X = H·S²·H`);
  `R_x(θ) = H·R_z(θ)·H` (`hadamardGate_comp_rotZGate_comp_hadamardGate`); and
  `R_x(-θ) = H·R_z(-θ)·H`. So the *only* non-`{H, S}` ingredient is the single base rotation
  `R_z(θ)` — the measurement-realised gate, whose reachability (Exercise 4.41/4.42) is the essential
  content of the exercise.
* `namedRotationTowerGates n θ` — **the named rotation tower submonoid.** The submonoid of
  `Evolution (qtower n qubit)` generated by the single-tower-wire placements of the three gates
  `hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ` (over every wire `i`). The tower counterpart of
  `Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`; a sub-submonoid of the full
  named four-gate tower submonoid.
* `qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates` — **the tower re-expression.** Every reachable
  rotation gate placed on a tower wire lies in the named rotation tower submonoid: for
  `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` and any wire `i`,

    `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E ∈ namedRotationTowerGates n θ`.

  Proved by `Submonoid.closure_induction` over the single-qubit re-expression:
  `qtowerSingleWire n i` is a monoid homomorphism (`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id` /
  `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp`), so
  it carries the closure `Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}` into the closure of
  the wire placements of `{hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`. This is exactly the rotation half of
  the containment `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ (named four-gate tower submonoid)` used in
  the universality theorem.

The rotation lifts are in `AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableWireSubmonoid.lean` and
`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableCircuitTower.lean`; `reachableRotationGates` and the `{H, S}`
conjugation lemmas are in `AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableRotation.lean`.
-/

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

/-- **The reachable single-qubit rotations are `{H, S}` circuits around `R_z(θ)`.** The reachable
single-qubit rotation submonoid `reachableRotationGates θ` (generated by `R_z(±θ), R_x(±θ)`) is
contained in the submonoid generated by the named gates `hadamardGate`, `sGate` together with the
single base rotation `rotZGate θ`:

  `reachableRotationGates θ ≤ Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`.

Each generator is a finite composition of `H`, `S`, `R_z(θ)`: `R_z(θ)` is itself a generator;
`R_z(-θ) = (H·S²·H)·R_z(θ)·(H·S²·H)` (`rotZGate_neg_eq_hadamardGate_sGate_conj`, with `NOT = H·S²·H`
the `{H, S}` realisation of the Pauli-`X`); `R_x(θ) = H·R_z(θ)·H`
(`hadamardGate_comp_rotZGate_comp_hadamardGate`); and `R_x(-θ) = H·R_z(-θ)·H`. Proved by
`Submonoid.closure_le`: it suffices that the four *generators* lie in the target submonoid; the unit
and products are then automatic. Only the single base rotation `R_z(θ)` — the measurement-realised
gate (Exercise 4.41) — is not itself an `{H, S}` word. -/
theorem reachableRotationGates_le_closure_named (θ : ℝ) :
    reachableRotationGates θ ≤
      Submonoid.closure ({hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ} : Set (Evolution qubit)) := by
  set G := Submonoid.closure ({hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ} : Set (Evolution qubit))
  have hH : hadamardGate ∈ G := Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
  have hS : sGate ∈ G := Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
  have hZ : rotZGate θ ∈ G := Submonoid.subset_closure (by simp)
  -- `NOT = H·S²·H ∈ G`; `Evolution.comp` is the monoid `*`, so `mul_mem` closes `.comp` goals.
  have hX : hadamardGate.comp ((sGate.comp sGate).comp hadamardGate) ∈ G :=
    mul_mem hH (mul_mem (mul_mem hS hS) hH)
  -- `R_z(-θ) = (H·S²·H)·R_z(θ)·(H·S²·H) ∈ G`.
  have hZneg : rotZGate (-θ) ∈ G := by
    rw [rotZGate_neg_eq_hadamardGate_sGate_conj]
    simp only [← Evolution.mul_def] at hX ⊢
    exact mul_mem hX (mul_mem hZ hX)
  -- `reachableRotationGates θ = Submonoid.closure {R_z(±θ), R_x(±θ)}`, so it suffices to place each
  -- of the four generators in `G`; the unit and products of `Submonoid.closure_le` are automatic.
  refine Submonoid.closure_le.2 ?_
  rintro x (rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl)
  · exact hZ
  · exact hZneg
  · rw [← hadamardGate_comp_rotZGate_comp_hadamardGate]
    exact mul_mem hH (mul_mem hZ hH)
  · rw [← hadamardGate_comp_rotZGate_comp_hadamardGate]
    exact mul_mem hH (mul_mem hZneg hH)

/-- **The named rotation tower submonoid.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qtower n qubit)` generated
by the single-tower-wire placements `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i g` of the three named gates
`g ∈ {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`, over every wire `i`. The tower counterpart of
`Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`, and the rotation part of the eventual full
named four-gate tower submonoid; every reachable rotation gate on a tower wire lies in it
(`qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates`). -/
noncomputable def namedRotationTowerGates (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    (⋃ i : Fin (n + 1),
      Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i ''
        ({hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ} : Set (Evolution qubit)))

/-- **Every reachable rotation gate on a tower wire is a named rotation tower gate.** For a
reachable single-qubit rotation gate `E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ` and any tower wire `i`, its
placement
`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E` lies in the named rotation tower submonoid
`namedRotationTowerGates n θ`.

The single-qubit re-expression `reachableRotationGates_le_closure_named` places `E` in
`Submonoid.closure {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`; then `Submonoid.closure_induction` transports
the word onto wire `i`, using that `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i` is a monoid homomorphism
(`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id` for the unit, `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp` for products) that
carries each generator `g ∈ {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}` to the generator
`Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i g` of `namedRotationTowerGates n θ`. This is the rotation half of
the containment `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ (named four-gate tower submonoid)`. -/
theorem qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates
    {n : ℕ} {θ : ℝ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) {E : Evolution qubit}
    (hE : E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ) :
    Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E ∈ namedRotationTowerGates n θ := by
  have hE' : E ∈ Submonoid.closure ({hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ} : Set (Evolution qubit)) :=
    reachableRotationGates_le_closure_named θ hE
  clear hE
  induction hE' using Submonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    exact Submonoid.subset_closure (Set.mem_iUnion.2 ⟨i, Set.mem_image_of_mem _ hx⟩)
  | one =>
    simpa only [Evolution.one_def, Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_id] using
      one_mem (namedRotationTowerGates n θ)
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
    rw [Evolution.mul_def, Evolution.qtowerSingleWire_comp, ← Evolution.mul_def]
    exact mul_mem ihx ihy

end

end AxQM
